description: Keep Node/npm and package-lock peers aligned with Azure Pipelines
alwaysApply: true
---

# Toolchain and lockfile (Azure alignment)

- Use the latest **Node 24.x** (current LTS) with its bundled **npm 11.x** (see `.nvmrc`, `engines`). Only the major is pinned — minor/patch float automatically, so don't set exact versions like `24.x.y` in `.nvmrc`, `engines`, the Dockerfile, or a `packageManager` field.
- Do not regenerate `package-lock.json` under a different Node/npm major (e.g. Node 26 / npm 12) — that can drop lockfile entries.
- Prefer `npm ci` after a clean clone (same as CI). Use `npm install` only when intentionally changing dependencies, still on the Node 24 / npm 11+ line.
- After any lockfile change, run `npm run check-toolchain` and ensure `package-lock.json` still contains `node_modules/react`, `node_modules/react-dom`, and `node_modules/scheduler` (Prisma Studio peers). Losing them breaks Azure `npm ci` (see PR #53 / commit `2e4f99d`).
- Keep those packages listed under root `optionalDependencies` so regenerating the lockfile does not drop them.
- Keep `overrides.preact` (`^10.29.8`) and `.npmrc` `legacy-peer-deps=false`. Do not enable legacy peer deps — it masks the accessible-autocomplete vs Defra map `preact` conflict that breaks Azure `npm ci`.
- Do not set `SKIP_TOOLCHAIN_CHECK=1` in normal PR work.
